window.MOCK_PAPER = {"title": "Exam 2 - PawPrint Dog Boarding", "subtitle": "A second full exam-format paper: a dog-boarding scenario with a Create boarding use case (create, loop and alt frames), a kiosk usability critique, a Loop partial DSD, ADO.NET code tracing and a summary report.", "summary": "100 marks &middot; 3 sections &middot; 3 hours (exam format).", "duration": 180, "sections": [{"key": "A", "title": "Section A - Multiple Choice Questions", "marks": 15, "color": "blue", "time": "about 40 minutes", "parts": [{"type": "mcq", "heading": "A - Multiple choice, Blocks 3 &amp; 4 (15 marks)", "start": 1, "intro": "Answer all 30 questions. Each question carries &frac12; mark (15 marks in total). The questions test reasoning rather than recall: you will trace code, diagnose a defect in a design, choose between competing designs and justify the choice. Read every option before answering, because several are plausible. Topics: the relational model and keys, normalisation, data types, the three-layer architecture and DSDs, ADO.NET, usability and UI design, and reporting.", "items": [["DOG(<u>DogID</u>, DogName, Breed, OwnerID) has OwnerID as a foreign key to OWNER. A clerk tries to delete owner 77 while three dogs still carry OwnerID 77, and the DBMS refuses. Which rule is protecting the data?", ["Entity integrity", "Domain integrity", "Referential integrity", "Normalisation"], 2, "Deleting the owner would leave three &lsquo;orphan&rsquo; dogs whose foreign key points at nothing. Referential integrity forces the dogs to be deleted or re-assigned first (or the delete to be cascaded by design)."], ["Which statement about a <b>foreign key</b> is correct?", ["It must be unique in the table that holds it", "It refers to a primary key in the parent table and may repeat in the child table", "It can never be NULL", "It must always be the first column of the table"], 1, "Many dogs may belong to one owner, so OwnerID repeats in DOG. It may be NULL when participation in the relationship is optional."], ["BOARDING_SERVICE has the composite primary key (BoardingNo, ServiceCode) and holds (101, GR). Which row can <b>not</b> be inserted next?", ["(101, WK)", "(102, GR)", "(101, GR) again, with a different Qty", "(103, WK)"], 2, "The <i>combination</i> must be unique. (101, WK) and (102, GR) re-use one value but form new combinations. A different Qty does not matter, because Qty is not part of the key."], ["Business rule: <i>a kennel can hold many boardings over time, and each boarding takes place in exactly one kennel</i>. Where does the foreign key go?", ["KENNEL gets a BoardingNo column", "BOARDING gets a KennelNo column", "A third table is always needed", "Both tables get a foreign key to each other"], 1, "In a one-to-many relationship the primary key of the &lsquo;one&rsquo; side (KENNEL) is copied into the &lsquo;many&rsquo; side (BOARDING) as a foreign key."], ["BOARDING_SHEET(<u>BoardingNo, ServiceCode</u>, ServiceName, Qty). ServiceCode &rarr; ServiceName. Assuming all values are atomic, what is the highest normal form of the table?", ["Unnormalised", "1NF", "2NF", "3NF"], 1, "ServiceName depends on only part of the composite key (ServiceCode): a partial dependency, so 2NF is violated and the table is in 1NF only."], ["OWNER(<u>OwnerID</u>, OwnerName, SuburbCode, SuburbName). SuburbCode &rarr; SuburbName. Which problem does this design cause?", ["A new suburb cannot be stored until at least one owner lives in it (insertion anomaly)", "An owner can have only one suburb", "OwnerID values will be duplicated", "The table violates 2NF because of a partial dependency"], 0, "SuburbName is determined by a non-key attribute: a transitive dependency (3NF violation). Because the key is a single column, a partial dependency is impossible, so 2NF is satisfied."], ["The primary key of BOARDING_SERVICE is (BoardingNo, ServiceCode). Which dependency is a <b>partial</b> dependency?", ["(BoardingNo, ServiceCode) &rarr; Qty", "BoardingNo &rarr; CheckInDate", "CheckInDate &rarr; BoardingNo", "Qty &rarr; ServiceCode"], 1, "A partial dependency is a non-key attribute depending on <i>part</i> of the key. BoardingNo alone determines CheckInDate. Qty depends on the whole key, a full dependency."], ["A table is already in 2NF. What <b>additional</b> condition must hold for it to be in 3NF?", ["Every attribute is atomic", "No non-key attribute depends on another non-key attribute", "The primary key must have one column", "There must be no foreign keys"], 1, "3NF removes transitive dependencies. Atomic values are the 1NF requirement."], ["The DOG table has a column <code class=\"inline\">Vaccinations</code> containing &lsquo;Rabies, Parvo, Distemper&rsquo;. What is the best fix?", ["Make the column wider", "Create a VACCINATION table with a DogID foreign key and one row per vaccination", "Add columns Vaccination1, Vaccination2 and Vaccination3 to DOG", "Store the list in a memo field"], 1, "A multi-valued attribute breaks 1NF. A repeating group of extra columns (Vaccination1, Vaccination2, &hellip;) is still poor design. A child table in a one-to-many relationship allows any number of vaccinations."], ["Which data type is the most appropriate for <code class=\"inline\">DogWeightKg</code> (for example 12.5)?", ["Integer", "Number with decimals (double / decimal)", "Short text", "Date/Time"], 1, "The value is a measured quantity with fractions, so use a decimal-capable numeric type. An integer would lose the .5."], ["A column <code class=\"inline\">DogName VARCHAR(30)</code> stores &lsquo;Rex&rsquo;. Which statement is correct?", ["It always occupies 30 bytes", "It uses space for the 3 characters plus a small length indicator, and a 31-character name will not fit", "The 30 is ignored by VARCHAR", "It can only hold digits"], 1, "VARCHAR is variable length with a declared maximum. The unused part of the 30 is not allocated; the maximum is still enforced."], ["Which attribute is best stored as a <b>Yes/No (Boolean)</b> field?", ["BoardingStatus (booked, checked in, completed, overdue)", "IsVaccinated (true / false)", "ServicePrice", "OwnerCell"], 1, "Boolean fits exactly two states. BoardingStatus has four values, so it needs text (or a lookup table)."], ["Which statement about the three-layer architecture is correct?", ["A Form may call a DomainClass directly to save time", "Forms call Handlers, Handlers call DomainClasses, and the database code is kept out of the Forms", "Handlers draw the screens", "DomainClasses call the Form to show results"], 1, "Layers depend downward: Form &rarr; Handler &rarr; DomainClass &rarr; database. The Form contains no SQL or business rules."], ["Which lifeline name is a correct <b>boundary</b> object in a DSD?", [":boardingHandler", ":CreateBoardingForm", ":Boarding", "Receptionist"], 1, "Boundary objects are forms or screens (suffix Form / UI / Page). <i>:boardingHandler</i> is the controller, <i>:Boarding</i> the entity and <i>Receptionist</i> the actor."], ["Which is the correct way to write the guard of a <b>loop</b> frame for &ldquo;for each service the owner selected&rdquo;?", ["[for each selected service]", "[if services &gt; 0]", "[else]", "[count = 0]"], 0, "A loop guard states what is iterated over. [if&hellip;] and [else] belong to opt and alt frames."], ["A DSD contains <code class=\"inline\">loop [for each service]</code> enclosing <code class=\"inline\">opt [service is in stock]</code> and the message <code class=\"inline\">reserveService()</code>. There are 4 services, of which 3 are in stock. How many times is the guard evaluated and the message sent?", ["Guard 3 times, message 3 times", "Guard 4 times, message 3 times", "Guard once, message 3 times", "Guard 4 times, message 4 times"], 1, "The loop body runs for every service (4), so the opt guard is tested 4 times; the message inside is sent only when the guard is true (3 times)."], ["<i>Create boarding</i> must first find the dog, using the steps of the <i>Search dog</i> use case. What is the best way to show this in the DSD?", ["Copy all the Search dog messages into the diagram", "Use a <b>ref</b> frame that names Search dog", "Use a loop frame around the search", "Leave it out, because searches are not shown"], 1, "A ref frame reuses another use case (an include relationship), so the behaviour is defined once and any change is made in one place."], ["Which statement about <code class=\"inline\">OleDbDataReader</code> is correct?", ["It loads the whole table into memory", "Read() moves to the next row and returns false when there are no more rows", "It can be used to INSERT rows", "It works without an open connection"], 1, "A data reader is a forward-only stream over an open connection. <code class=\"inline\">while (rdr.Read())</code> loops until Read() returns false."], ["A single-row <code class=\"inline\">INSERT</code> succeeds. What does <code class=\"inline\">ExecuteNonQuery()</code> return?", ["0", "1", "true", "The new primary key value"], 1, "ExecuteNonQuery returns the number of rows affected: 1 for one inserted row. It does not return the key and it is not a Boolean."], ["<code class=\"inline\">SELECT ServicePrice FROM SERVICE WHERE ServiceCode = ?</code> matches no row. What does <code class=\"inline\">ExecuteScalar()</code> return?", ["0", "An empty string", "null", "It throws an OleDbException"], 2, "With no rows ExecuteScalar returns a null reference, so code should test <code class=\"inline\">if (price == null)</code> before casting."], ["What is the purpose of an <code class=\"inline\">OleDbDataAdapter</code>?", ["To fill a DataSet / DataTable with the result of a query so it can be worked with while disconnected", "To open the connection", "To execute INSERT statements one row at a time", "To validate user input"], 0, "The adapter bridges the database and an in-memory DataSet/DataTable. The connection opens the channel and the command carries the SQL."], ["A method has <code class=\"inline\">return &quot;No such service&quot;;</code> inside its <code class=\"inline\">try</code> block, and a <code class=\"inline\">finally { conn.Close(); }</code> block. What happens?", ["finally is skipped because the method has already returned", "finally runs first, then the method returns", "A compile error", "The connection stays open"], 1, "A finally block always executes when control leaves the try, including via return, so the connection is closed."], ["A kiosk screen shows 14 fields, a flashing promotion and three different fonts at once. Which Nielsen heuristic is mainly violated?", ["Aesthetic and minimalist design", "Error prevention", "Visibility of system status", "Match between the system and the real world"], 0, "Extra, irrelevant or competing information dilutes the information that matters. Keep only what the task needs."], ["Owners must remember kennel codes seen on an earlier screen and type them later. Which Shneiderman rule is broken?", ["Strive for consistency", "Reduce short-term memory load", "Permit easy reversal of actions", "Enable frequent users to use shortcuts"], 1, "People hold only a few items in short-term memory. Show choices (lists, defaults) so the user recognises instead of recalls."], ["Which control is best for capturing the <b>check-in date</b>?", ["TextBox with a format hint", "DateTimePicker", "ComboBox with typed values", "NumericUpDown"], 1, "A DateTimePicker removes format errors and can restrict the range (for example MinDate = today)."], ["A receptionist must be able to tick <b>any number</b> of services (grooming, walks, training). Which control fits?", ["RadioButtons", "A group of CheckBoxes or a CheckedListBox", "A single ComboBox", "A read-only Label"], 1, "Zero or many independent choices call for check boxes. Radio buttons and a single-selection ComboBox allow only one choice."], ["Which is the best wording for an inline validation message when the check-out date is before the check-in date?", ["Invalid input", "Error 5", "Check-out date must be on or after the check-in date.", "You entered the wrong date."], 2, "A good message is plain, specific, constructive and placed next to the field. &ldquo;Invalid input&rdquo; and codes give no help, and the last option blames the user without helping."], ["A report shows the number of boardings per month for the last 12 months as a line chart. Which type is it?", ["Exception report", "Trend / comparative report", "Detail transaction report", "Audit report"], 1, "Changes over time are shown by a trend (comparative) report, typically a line chart with time on the x-axis."], ["Which is the best statement of a report&rsquo;s <b>recipient</b>?", ["Everyone", "The Operations Manager", "The database", "Management in general"], 1, "Name a specific role who can act on the report. &ldquo;Everyone&rdquo; or &ldquo;management&rdquo; are too vague to judge usefulness."], ["Which of the following is a <b>derived</b> field in a report?", ["KennelNo", "DailyRate", "Revenue = Nights &times; DailyRate", "CheckInDate"], 2, "A derived field is calculated when the report is run (not stored). The other three are stored attributes."]]}]}, {"key": "B", "title": "Section B - Interaction Design, Usability &amp; UI Scenario", "marks": 17, "color": "yellow", "time": "about 35 minutes", "parts": [{"type": "qs", "heading": "Question B - Interaction design, usability principles and UI design (17 marks)", "scenario": "PawPrint Dog Boarding has installed a self-service <b>kiosk</b> in reception on which an <b>owner</b> books a stay for a registered dog. Figure B shows version 1 of the <i>Book a Stay</i> screen. Observations from a pilot with 30 owners:<ul><li>Twelve fields, a flashing &ldquo;50% OFF GROOMING!!&rdquo; banner and three different fonts appear on one screen. The <b>Next</b> button is pale grey on a grey background.</li><li>The owner must type the dog&rsquo;s name exactly; &ldquo;rex&rdquo; is not found when the record says &ldquo;Rex&rdquo;. Regular owners must re-enter the dog, and all their details, on every visit.</li><li>Services are typed as codes separated by commas (for example <code class=\"inline\">GR,WK</code>). The meaning of the codes is printed on a poster next to the kiosk.</li><li>If the check-out date is earlier than the check-in date, a pop-up reading <b>&ldquo;Invalid input&rdquo;</b> appears on the <i>last</i> page, without saying which field is wrong.</li><li>The button that moves the owner forward is called <b>Next</b> on page 1, <b>Finish</b> on page 2 and <b>Done</b> on page 3, and it moves around the screen.</li><li>The kiosk wipes everything after 60 seconds of inactivity and there is no Back button. After <b>Done</b> the kiosk returns to a blank welcome screen with no booking number.</li></ul>", "diagram": "<div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 720 380\" width=\"720\" height=\"380\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Figure B: Book a Stay kiosk screen, version 1\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"720\" height=\"380\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Figure B: Book a Stay screen (version 1), owner self-service kiosk</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"680\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"680\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">PawPrint Kiosk 1.0</text><text x=\"686\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">✕</text><rect x=\"21\" y=\"65\" width=\"678\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#ffe100\" stroke=\"#ffe100\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#c00\">50% OFF GROOMING!!  50% OFF GROOMING!!  50% OFF GROOMING!!</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Dog</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"106\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"121\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#777\" font-style=\"italic\">type name here</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Knl sz (1/2/3)</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"138\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">2</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">In</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"170\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#777\" font-style=\"italic\">yyyy/m/d</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Out</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"202\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#777\" font-style=\"italic\">yyyy/m/d</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Svc (e.g. GR,WK)</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"234\" width=\"200\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"249\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">GR,WK</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Type the dog's name exactly</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">1 = S, 2 = M, 3 = L (see poster)</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"283\" font-size=\"8.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">GR grooming  WK walk  TR training (see poster)</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"300\" width=\"100\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#e4e4e4\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"610\" y=\"316\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#cfcfcf\">Next &gt;&gt;</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"332\" width=\"300\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fff0f0\" stroke=\"#d99\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"347\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#c00\">Invalid input</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"347\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#777\">Session ends in 00:12</text></svg></div>", "qs": [{"id": "B1", "marks": 5, "q": "Name the <b>Nielsen usability heuristic</b> that is violated by each of the following observations. [1 mark each]<br>(i) Twelve fields, a flashing banner and three fonts on one screen.<br>(ii) The message &ldquo;Invalid input&rdquo;.<br>(iii) Service codes must be remembered from a poster.<br>(iv) Regular owners must re-enter the dog and all their details at every visit.<br>(v) The dog name must be typed exactly, otherwise the dog is &ldquo;not found&rdquo;.", "a": "<table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Heuristic violated</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(i)</td><td><b>Aesthetic and minimalist design</b></td><td>Irrelevant and competing information (banner, fonts, 12 fields) distracts from the task.</td></tr><tr><td>(ii)</td><td><b>Help users recognise, diagnose and recover from errors</b></td><td>The message does not say which field is wrong, why, or how to fix it.</td></tr><tr><td>(iii)</td><td><b>Recognition rather than recall</b></td><td>The owner must remember codes instead of choosing from a visible list.</td></tr><tr><td>(iv)</td><td><b>Flexibility and efficiency of use</b></td><td>No saved details, defaults or shortcuts for frequent users.</td></tr><tr><td>(v)</td><td><b>Error prevention</b></td><td>Free-text matching invites mistakes; a list of the owner&rsquo;s dogs would prevent them.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>1 mark per heuristic. Accept a defensible alternative (for example <i>Recognition rather than recall</i> for (v)).</p>"}, {"id": "B2", "marks": 4, "q": "Name the <b>Shneiderman golden rule</b> broken by each observation and give <b>one</b> design change that fixes it. [&frac12; + &frac12; each]<br>(a) The kiosk wipes the screen after 60 seconds and there is no Back button.<br>(b) The forward button is called Next, Finish and Done on three pages.<br>(c) After Done the kiosk returns to a blank welcome screen.<br>(d) The date error is reported only on the last page.", "a": "<table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Golden rule</th><th>Acceptable fix (any one)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td><b>Support internal locus of control</b> (also: <i>Permit easy reversal of actions</i>)</td><td>Add Back and Cancel buttons; warn before time-out and let the owner continue.</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td><b>Strive for consistency</b></td><td>One label (for example <i>Continue</i>), one place and one colour for the primary button.</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td><b>Design dialogs to yield closure</b></td><td>A summary page: &ldquo;Booking 2417 confirmed for Rex, 20&ndash;25 October&rdquo; with a clear end.</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td><b>Offer error prevention and simple error handling</b></td><td>Restrict check-out with DateTimePicker MinDate; validate when the field loses focus (ErrorProvider).</td></tr></tbody></table><p>&frac12; for the rule and &frac12; for a sensible fix, per part.</p>"}, {"id": "B3", "marks": 4, "q": "Redesign the form. For each item name the <b>best Windows Forms control</b> and justify it.<br>(a) The dog (the DOG table has DogID, DogName and Breed; the owner is already logged in). State the <code class=\"inline\">DisplayMember</code> and <code class=\"inline\">ValueMember</code>. [2]<br>(b) The services required (SERVICE has ServiceCode, ServiceName, ServicePrice). [1]<br>(c) The check-in and check-out dates. [1]", "a": "<p><b>(a)</b> <b>ComboBox</b> (DropDownList) listing <i>only the logged-in owner&rsquo;s dogs</i> &#10003;. <code class=\"inline\">DisplayMember = \"DogName\"</code> and <code class=\"inline\">ValueMember = \"DogID\"</code> &#10003; so the owner sees names and the program gets the foreign key. No typing means no &ldquo;dog not found&rdquo; errors &#10003;.</p><p><b>(b)</b> <b>CheckedListBox</b> (or a group of CheckBoxes) filled from SERVICE: DisplayMember = ServiceName, ValueMember = ServiceCode &#10003;. Zero or many independent choices; no codes to remember.</p><p><b>(c)</b> Two <b>DateTimePickers</b> &#10003; with MinDate = today for check-in and MinDate = check-in date for check-out, so the invalid combination cannot be entered.</p><p>Model wireframe (illustration):</p><div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 360\" width=\"900\" height=\"360\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Redesigned Book a Stay form\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"900\" height=\"360\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Wireframe: Book a Stay form, version 2 (model answer)</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"540\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"540\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">PawPrint - Book a Stay</text><text x=\"546\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">✕</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Dog *</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"78\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Rex (Labrador)</text><rect x=\"416\" y=\"78\" width=\"24\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">▾</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Check-in date *</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"116\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">20 October 2026</text><rect x=\"416\" y=\"116\" width=\"24\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">▾</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Check-out date *</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"154\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">15 October 2026</text><rect x=\"416\" y=\"154\" width=\"24\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"428\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">▾</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Services</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"194\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"197\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">✓</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Grooming (R150)</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"216\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"212\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Daily walk (R60)</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"238\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"212\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Training (R200)</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Kennel</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#555\">Assigned by the system: Medium</text><rect x=\"190\" y=\"312\" width=\"150\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#cfe3ff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" rx=\"5\"/><text x=\"265\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Confirm Booking</text><rect x=\"352\" y=\"312\" width=\"90\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#f2f4f8\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" rx=\"5\"/><text x=\"397\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Cancel</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">ComboBox: DisplayMember = DogName</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">ValueMember = DogID (FK)</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">DateTimePicker, MinDate = today</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#b3261e\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Out &lt; In: ErrorProvider icon + message here</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">CheckedListBox / CheckBoxes from SERVICE</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">(Display = ServiceName, Value = ServiceCode)</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"327\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0b7a3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Verb-based buttons; Cancel keeps control</text></svg></div>"}, {"id": "B4", "marks": 4, "q": "Feedback and error handling.<br>(a) Write the exact text of the <b>inline error message</b> for a check-out date that is earlier than the check-in date, and say where it appears. [2]<br>(b) Replace Next / Finish / Done with two action-oriented button labels and say where they belong. [1]<br>(c) Write the exact confirmation message shown after a successful booking. [1]", "a": "<p><b>(a)</b> Example: <i>&ldquo;Check-out date must be on or after the check-in date.&rdquo;</i> &#10003; (plain, specific, tells the owner how to fix it). Shown by an <b>ErrorProvider</b> icon <b>next to the check-out field</b> as soon as the field loses focus, not in a generic pop-up on the last page &#10003;.</p><p><b>(b)</b> <b>[Confirm Booking]</b> (primary, bottom-right, default) and <b>[Cancel]</b> (secondary, beside it) &#10003;.</p><p><b>(c)</b> Example: <i>&ldquo;Booking 2417 confirmed: Rex, Medium kennel, 20 to 25 October.&rdquo;</i> &#10003; (booking number, dog and dates; displayed at the end of the dialog, then a clear next step).</p>"}]}]}, {"key": "C", "title": "Section C - Comprehensive Case Scenario", "marks": 68, "color": "green", "time": "about 105 minutes", "parts": [{"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C1 - Database design and ERD (16 marks)", "scenario": "<b>PawPrint Dog Boarding</b> looks after dogs while their owners are away. <i>Owners</i> are identified by a system-generated OwnerID and have a name and a cell number. <i>Dogs</i> have a system-generated DogID, a name and a breed. A dog belongs to exactly one owner, an owner may register many dogs, and an owner may be registered before any dog is added. <i>Kennels</i> have a KennelNo, a size (&ldquo;small&rdquo;, &ldquo;medium&rdquo; or &ldquo;large&rdquo;) and a daily rate. A <i>boarding</i> is one stay of one dog in one kennel: it has a system-generated BoardingNo, a check-in date, a check-out date and a status (&ldquo;booked&rdquo; when created, then &ldquo;checked in&rdquo;, &ldquo;completed&rdquo; or &ldquo;overdue&rdquo;). A kennel is used by many boardings over time. <i>Services</i> (for example grooming, daily walk, training) have a ServiceCode, a name and a price. A boarding may include many services and a service may be used on many boardings; for each one the quantity (Qty) is recorded. The only user role in the system is a receptionist.", "diagram": "<div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1330 400\" width=\"1330\" height=\"400\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Domain class diagram\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1330\" height=\"400\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"665\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Domain class diagram: PawPrint Dog Boarding</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"50\" width=\"220\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"50\" width=\"220\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Owner</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerID</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerName</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerCell</text><rect x=\"360\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"360\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"465\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Dog</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogID</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogName</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Breed</text><rect x=\"700\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"122\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"700\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"805\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Boarding</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingNo</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">CheckInDate</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">CheckOutDate</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingStatus</text><rect x=\"1090\" y=\"61\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"1090\" y=\"61\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1195\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Service</text><text x=\"1100\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceCode</text><text x=\"1100\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceName</text><text x=\"1100\" y=\"147\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServicePrice</text><rect x=\"700\" y=\"270\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"700\" y=\"270\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"805\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Kennel</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"312\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelNo</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"334\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelSize</text><text x=\"710\" y=\"356\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DailyRate</text><polyline points=\"240,100 300,100 300,100 360,100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"248\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">1..1</text><text x=\"352\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">owns</text><polyline points=\"570,100 635,100 635,111 700,111\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"578\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">1..1</text><text x=\"692\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"635\" y=\"105.5\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">stays in</text><polyline points=\"805,270 805,221 805,221 805,172\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"813\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">1..1</text><text x=\"813\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"805\" y=\"237\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">houses</text><polyline points=\"910,111 1000,111 1000,111 1090,111\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"918\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"1082\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">0..*</text><text x=\"1000\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">includes</text><rect x=\"945\" y=\"190\" width=\"120\" height=\"78\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"945\" y=\"190\" width=\"120\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1005\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingService</text><text x=\"955\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Qty</text><line x1=\"1000\" y1=\"111\" x2=\"1000\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/></svg></div>", "qs": [{"id": "C1.1", "marks": 9, "q": "Using the domain class diagram above, draw a fully labelled <b>entity relationship diagram (ERD)</b> for the database. Include <b>all attributes</b>, primary keys, foreign keys and the cardinality of every relationship. Resolve any many-to-many relationship. Table names must be in capital letters.", "a": "<p>The many-to-many relationship between BOARDING and SERVICE is resolved with the bridge table <b>BOARDING_SERVICE</b>, which takes the primary keys of both parents (as a composite key and as foreign keys) and the attribute of the association class (Qty).</p><div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1350 440\" width=\"1350\" height=\"440\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ERD (model answer): PawPrint Dog Boarding\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1350\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"675\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ERD (model answer): PawPrint Dog Boarding</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"50\" width=\"210\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OWNER</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerID</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerName</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerCell</text><rect x=\"350\" y=\"50\" width=\"220\" height=\"122\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"350\" y=\"50\" width=\"220\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"460\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DOG</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogID</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogName</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Breed</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">FK</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">OwnerID</text><rect x=\"690\" y=\"50\" width=\"240\" height=\"166\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"690\" y=\"50\" width=\"240\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BOARDING</text><text x=\"698\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingNo</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">CheckInDate</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">CheckOutDate</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingStatus</text><text x=\"698\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">FK</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DogID</text><text x=\"698\" y=\"202\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">FK</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"202\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelNo</text><rect x=\"1070\" y=\"50\" width=\"250\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"1070\" y=\"50\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1195\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BOARDING_SERVICE</text><text x=\"1078\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK,FK</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">BoardingNo</text><text x=\"1078\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK,FK</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceCode</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Qty</text><rect x=\"1070\" y=\"300\" width=\"250\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"1070\" y=\"300\" width=\"250\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1195\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">SERVICE</text><text x=\"1078\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceCode</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"364\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServiceName</text><text x=\"1130\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ServicePrice</text><rect x=\"690\" y=\"300\" width=\"240\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"690\" y=\"300\" width=\"240\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KENNEL</text><text x=\"698\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">PK</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelNo</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"364\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KennelSize</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">DailyRate</text><polyline points=\"230,100 290,100 290,111 350,111\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"238\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"342\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"105.5\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">owns</text><polyline points=\"570,111 630,111 630,133 690,133\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"578\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"682\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"630\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">stays in</text><polyline points=\"810,300 810,258 810,258 810,216\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"818\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"818\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">houses</text><polyline points=\"930,133 1000,133 1000,100 1070,100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"938\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"1062\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"1000\" y=\"116.5\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">includes</text><polyline points=\"1195,300 1195,225 1195,225 1195,150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1203\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">1..1</text><text x=\"1203\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">0..*</text><text x=\"1195\" y=\"241\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">is used in</text></svg></div><p><b>Marking guide</b></p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Award marks for</th><th>Marks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Six tables with correct names (OWNER, DOG, KENNEL, BOARDING, SERVICE, BOARDING_SERVICE): 5 correct = &frac12;, all six including the bridge = 2</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>All attributes present and in the correct table; no methods</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Primary keys: OwnerID, DogID, KennelNo, BoardingNo, ServiceCode; BOARDING_SERVICE composite (BoardingNo, ServiceCode)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Foreign keys: DOG.OwnerID, BOARDING.DogID, BOARDING.KennelNo, BOARDING_SERVICE.BoardingNo, BOARDING_SERVICE.ServiceCode</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Cardinalities on all five relationships, with the 1..1 end at the parent</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><b>Total</b></td><td><b>9</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"}, {"id": "C1.2", "marks": 3, "q": "(a) Write the business rule, in a full sentence, that the <i>Owner&ndash;Dog</i> relationship expresses, and the one that the <i>Kennel&ndash;Boarding</i> relationship expresses. [1 each]<br>(b) Explain why the ERD needs the table BOARDING_SERVICE although the business describes only boardings and services. [1]", "a": "<p><b>(a)</b> Owner&ndash;Dog: <i>&ldquo;An owner may register many dogs (or none yet), but each dog belongs to exactly one owner.&rdquo;</i> &#10003;<br>Kennel&ndash;Boarding: <i>&ldquo;A kennel is used by many boardings over time (possibly none yet), but each boarding takes place in exactly one kennel.&rdquo;</i> &#10003;</p><p><b>(b)</b> A relational table cannot hold a many-to-many relationship directly: a boarding has many services and a service is used on many boardings. The bridge table turns it into two one-to-many relationships and is where the Qty of each service on each boarding is stored &#10003;.</p>"}, {"id": "C1.3", "marks": 4, "q": "The receptionist currently records service use in a spreadsheet. Study the sample rows below. The primary key is the <b>composite (BoardingNo, ServiceCode)</b>. The dependencies are ServiceCode &rarr; ServiceName, ServicePrice and BoardingNo &rarr; CheckInDate.<br><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>BoardingNo</th><th>ServiceCode</th><th>ServiceName</th><th>ServicePrice</th><th>Qty</th><th>CheckInDate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>101</td><td>GR</td><td>Grooming</td><td>150</td><td>1</td><td>2026/10/05</td></tr><tr><td>101</td><td>WK</td><td>Daily walk</td><td>60</td><td>3</td><td>2026/10/05</td></tr><tr><td>102</td><td>GR</td><td>Grooming</td><td>150</td><td>2</td><td>2026/10/07</td></tr></tbody></table></div>(a) State the highest normal form the table is in. [1]<br>(b) Name the type of dependency that causes the problem. [1]<br>(c) Normalise the table to third normal form. Redraw the tables and underline the primary keys. [2]", "a": "<p><b>(a)</b> <b>1NF</b> &#10003; (all values atomic, but there are partial dependencies, so 2NF is violated).</p><p><b>(b)</b> <b>Partial dependencies</b> &#10003;: ServiceName and ServicePrice depend on ServiceCode only, and CheckInDate depends on BoardingNo only, each a part of the composite key. Only Qty depends on the whole key.</p><p><b>(c)</b> (&frac12; per table, &frac12; for keys/FKs):</p><ul><li>BOARDING (<u>BoardingNo</u>, CheckInDate)</li><li>SERVICE (<u>ServiceCode</u>, ServiceName, ServicePrice)</li><li>BOARDING_SERVICE (<u>BoardingNo, ServiceCode</u>, Qty)</li></ul><p>BoardingNo and ServiceCode in BOARDING_SERVICE are foreign keys. The price of grooming is now stored once. Each table is also in 3NF (no transitive dependencies remain).</p>"}]}, {"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C2 - Use case realisation (25 marks)", "scenario": "The following flow of activities has been developed for the <i>Create boarding</i> use case.<div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Actor</th><th>System</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1. Requests to create boarding</td><td>1.1 Prompts for DogID, KennelNo, check-in date, check-out date and the service codes required (zero or more)</td></tr><tr><td>2. Enters DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate and the service codes</td><td>2.1 Invokes <i>Search dog</i> use case to display the dog&rsquo;s name and owner<br><br>2.2 Uses KennelNo, CheckInDate and CheckOutDate to check whether the kennel is available (no overlapping boarding exists for those dates)<br><br><i>If the kennel is available</i><br>2.3 Receives a newly generated BoardingNo from the database management system and creates a new boarding in the BOARDING table, including BoardingNo, DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate and BoardingStatus = &ldquo;booked&rdquo;<br><br>2.4 For each service code: uses ServiceCode to retrieve the ServiceName from the SERVICE table and creates a new BoardingService record (BoardingNo, ServiceCode, Qty = 1)<br><br>2.5 Confirms creation of the boarding and displays the BoardingNo</td></tr><tr><td><i>Extensions</i></td><td><i>If the kennel is not available</i><br>2.3 Displays &ldquo;Kennel not available for those dates&rdquo; and does not create a boarding</td></tr></tbody></table></div>", "qs": [{"id": "C2.1", "marks": 18, "q": "Draw and fully label a <b>design sequence diagram</b> (three-layer: boundary, controller and entity objects) to realise the <i>Create boarding</i> use case. Include the <b>extension</b> and any <b>interaction frames</b> you need. Objects that are created during the use case must be drawn where they are created.", "a": "<p>Model answer (any equivalent, consistently named design earns full marks; for example the new boarding may return BoardingNo as a dashed return or a variable assignment, and the kennel check may be a count of overlapping boardings sent to :Boarding):</p><div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1525 904\" width=\"1525\" height=\"904\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sequence Diagram: Create Boarding\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1525\" height=\"904\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"95\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"515\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"730\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"730\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"945\" y1=\"510\" x2=\"945\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"1160\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"1160\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"1375\" y1=\"668\" x2=\"1375\" y2=\"888\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><rect x=\"221.5\" y=\"56\" width=\"157\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:CreateBoardingForm</text><rect x=\"447\" y=\"56\" width=\"136\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"515\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:boardingHandler</text><rect x=\"682\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"730\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:Kennel</text><rect x=\"897\" y=\"482\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"945\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:Boarding</text><rect x=\"1112\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1160\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:Service</text><rect x=\"1307\" y=\"640\" width=\"136\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"1375\" y=\"658\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\">:BoardingService</text><rect x=\"252\" y=\"444\" width=\"1226\" height=\"360\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M252 444 h42 v13 l-8 9 h-34 z\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"258\" y=\"459\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">alt</text><text x=\"306\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">[available = true]</text><line x1=\"252\" y1=\"724\" x2=\"1478\" y2=\"724\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 4\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"738\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">[available = false]</text><rect x=\"481\" y=\"562\" width=\"983\" height=\"110\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M481 562 h50 v13 l-8 9 h-42 z\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"487\" y=\"577\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">loop</text><text x=\"543\" y=\"578\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">[for each service code]</text><text x=\"762.5\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Sequence Diagram: Create Boarding</text><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"64\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"71\" x2=\"95\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"83\" y1=\"78\" x2=\"107\" y2=\"78\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"85\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"105\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"95\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Receptionist</text><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"298\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"197.5\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">requestCreateBoarding()</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"97\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"197.5\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">promptForDetails()</text><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"298\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"197.5\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">enterDetails(DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate, serviceCodes)</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"513\" y2=\"320\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"407.5\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">createBoarding(DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate, serviceCodes)</text><rect x=\"475\" y=\"330\" width=\"295\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M475 330 h34 v11 l-7 8 h-27 z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"481\" y=\"343\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">ref</text><text x=\"634.5\" y=\"352\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Search dog</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"418\" x2=\"728\" y2=\"418\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"622.5\" y=\"412\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">available := checkAvailability(KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate)</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"496\" x2=\"895\" y2=\"496\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"706\" y=\"490\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">createBoarding(DogID, KennelNo, CheckInDate, CheckOutDate, &quot;booked&quot;)</text><line x1=\"945\" y1=\"536\" x2=\"517\" y2=\"536\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"730\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">BoardingNo</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"610\" x2=\"1158\" y2=\"610\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"837.5\" y=\"604\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">name := getServiceName(ServiceCode)</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"654\" x2=\"1305\" y2=\"654\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"911\" y=\"648\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">createBoardingService(BoardingNo, ServiceCode, 1)</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"712\" x2=\"302\" y2=\"712\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"407.5\" y=\"706\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">confirmation(BoardingNo)</text><line x1=\"515\" y1=\"786\" x2=\"302\" y2=\"786\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"407.5\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">kennelUnavailable</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"844\" x2=\"97\" y2=\"844\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"197.5\" y=\"838\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">displayMessage(text)</text></svg></div><p><b>Marking guide</b></p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Award marks for</th><th>Marks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Notation: actor as stick figure top-left; lifelines in rectangles, prefixed with a colon and underlined; solid filled-head requests; dashed open-head returns</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Boundary <i>:CreateBoardingForm</i> and controller <i>:boardingHandler</i> both present and correctly named and placed</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Existing entities <i>:Kennel</i> and <i>:Service</i> at the top; new entities <i>:Boarding</i> and <i>:BoardingService</i> drawn lower, at their point of creation</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Actor &rarr; Form requests, Form &rarr; Handler with all parameters including the service codes</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td><b>ref</b> frame <i>Search dog</i></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Availability check sent to :Kennel with the result returned or assigned</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>alt</b> frame with both guards ([available = true] / [available = false]) and a dashed divider</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Creation of :Boarding: arrow from the Handler pointing at the new box (not the lifeline) with the parameters including status &ldquo;booked&rdquo;; BoardingNo returned</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td><b>loop</b> frame with a guard ([for each service code]) nested in the first alt branch</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Inside the loop: the service lookup to :Service and the creation of :BoardingService</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Confirmation / unavailable returns and the final message to the actor</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Total</b></td><td><b>18</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"}, {"id": "C2.2", "marks": 3, "q": "Write down the <b>post-conditions</b> for the <i>Create boarding</i> use case: two for a successful booking and one for the extension. [1 each]", "a": "<ul><li><b>Success 1:</b> A new BOARDING record exists with a system-generated BoardingNo, the entered DogID, KennelNo and dates, and BoardingStatus = &ldquo;booked&rdquo;. &#10003;</li><li><b>Success 2:</b> One BOARDING_SERVICE record exists for every service code that was selected, linked to the new BoardingNo. &#10003;</li><li><b>Extension (kennel unavailable):</b> No BOARDING or BOARDING_SERVICE record is created and the receptionist is told that the kennel is not available. &#10003;</li></ul>"}, {"id": "C2.3", "marks": 2, "q": "List <b>two pre-conditions</b> for the <i>Create boarding</i> use case. [1 each]", "a": "<p>Any two (&#10003; each): the receptionist is logged in; the dog is already registered (and so is its owner); the kennel exists; the service codes entered exist in the SERVICE table; the database is available.</p>"}, {"id": "C2.4", "marks": 2, "q": "The use case <i>Create boarding</i> invokes <i>Search dog</i> instead of repeating its steps. Explain why this is good design and name the relationship between the two use cases. [2]", "a": "<p>The search steps are defined once and reused by several use cases (for example Create boarding and Update dog), so a change is made in one place and the diagrams stay consistent and shorter &#10003;. The relationship is <b>&laquo;include&raquo;</b> (shown in the DSD with a ref frame) &#10003;.</p>"}]}, {"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C3 - Partial sequence diagram (8 marks)", "scenario": "Every morning the receptionist runs <i>Flag overdue boardings</i>. A boarding is <b>overdue</b> when its check-out date is earlier than today&rsquo;s date and its status is still &ldquo;checked in&rdquo;. The handler asks the BOARDING class for the list of overdue boardings for today&rsquo;s date and then sets the status of <b>each</b> boarding in that list to &ldquo;overdue&rdquo;. Study the partial sequence diagram below (the use case is started by a timer or by another use case, so there is no boundary object).", "diagram": "<div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 810 432\" width=\"810\" height=\"432\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Partial Sequence Diagram: Flag Overdue Boardings\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"810\" height=\"432\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"416\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"660\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"660\" y2=\"416\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><rect x=\"312\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(a)</tspan></text><rect x=\"612\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"660\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(b)</tspan></text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"266\" width=\"368\" height=\"66\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M326 266 h42 v13 l-8 9 h-34 z\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"332\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(e)</tspan></text><text x=\"380\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(f)</tspan></text><text x=\"405\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Partial Sequence Diagram: Flag Overdue Boardings</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"358\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">requestFlagOverdue(<tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(c)</tspan>)</text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"658\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">overdueList := <tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(d)</tspan></text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"314\" x2=\"658\" y2=\"314\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(g)</tspan></text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"372\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"372\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"366\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a4b00\">(h)</tspan></text></svg></div>", "qs": [{"id": "C3.1", "marks": 8, "q": "Supply the missing labels that correspond to (a) to (h). [1 mark each]<br><b>Note:</b> You do NOT have to redraw the sequence diagram.", "a": "<div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Label</th><th>Answer</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td><b>:boardingHandler</b></td><td>The controller that receives the request and sends every other message.</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td><b>:Boarding</b></td><td>The entity that supplies the list of overdue boardings and whose status is updated.</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td><b>CurrentDate</b></td><td>The parameter of the request; it is the same date passed to <i>getOverdueBoardings</i> (&ldquo;today&rsquo;s date&rdquo;).</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td><b>getOverdueBoardings(CurrentDate)</b></td><td>A search message that returns a list, stored in <i>overdueList</i> (verb-noun, camelCase).</td></tr><tr><td>(e)</td><td><b>Loop</b></td><td>The same step is repeated for <b>each</b> boarding in the list, so the frame is a Loop (not Opt or Alt).</td></tr><tr><td>(f)</td><td><b>[for each boarding in overdueList]</b></td><td>The loop guard states what is iterated over, taken from the scenario.</td></tr><tr><td>(g)</td><td><b>setBoardingStatus(BoardingNo, &ldquo;overdue&rdquo;)</b></td><td>Update message from the controller to :Boarding, sent once per iteration. Accept <i>updateStatus(&ldquo;overdue&rdquo;)</i>.</td></tr><tr><td>(h)</td><td><b>confirmation</b></td><td>Dashed return to the caller after the loop has finished. Accept <i>return confirmation</i>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>Completed diagram (answers in green):</b></p><div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 810 432\" width=\"810\" height=\"432\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Partial Sequence Diagram: Flag Overdue Boardings\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"810\" height=\"432\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"416\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><line x1=\"660\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"660\" y2=\"416\" stroke=\"#7d889b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\"/><rect x=\"292\" y=\"56\" width=\"136\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">:boardingHandler</tspan></text><rect x=\"612\" y=\"56\" width=\"96\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"660\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\" text-decoration=\"underline\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">:Boarding</tspan></text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"266\" width=\"368\" height=\"66\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><path d=\"M326 266 h50 v13 l-8 9 h-42 z\" fill=\"#eef2fa\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"332\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">Loop</tspan></text><text x=\"388\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1b2230\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">[for each boarding in overdueList]</tspan></text><text x=\"405\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Partial Sequence Diagram: Flag Overdue Boardings</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"358\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">requestFlagOverdue(<tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">CurrentDate</tspan>)</text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"658\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">overdueList := <tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">getOverdueBoardings(CurrentDate)</tspan></text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"314\" x2=\"658\" y2=\"314\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"510\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">setBoardingStatus(BoardingNo, &quot;overdue&quot;)</tspan></text><line x1=\"360\" y1=\"372\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"372\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#ao)\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"366\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\" font-style=\"italic\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><tspan fill=\"#0b7a3b\" font-weight=\"700\">confirmation</tspan></text></svg></div>"}]}, {"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C4 - ADO.NET code analysis (7 marks)", "scenario": "The <i>BoardingHandler</i> contains the method below. BOARDING 101 exists, and the tables hold the rows shown. ServicePrice is a whole number (Long Integer) and (BoardingNo, ServiceCode) is the primary key of BOARDING_SERVICE.<div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>ServiceCode</th><th>ServiceName</th><th>ServicePrice</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GR</td><td>Grooming</td><td>150</td></tr><tr><td>WK</td><td>Daily walk</td><td>60</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>BoardingNo</th><th>ServiceCode</th><th>Qty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>101</td><td>GR</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><pre class=\"sql\">public string addService(int boardingNo, string serviceCode, int qty)\n{\n    string msg = &quot;&quot;;\n    OleDbConnection conn = new OleDbConnection(connString);\n    try\n    {\n        conn.Open();\n        OleDbCommand chk = new OleDbCommand(\n          &quot;SELECT ServicePrice FROM SERVICE WHERE ServiceCode = ?&quot;, conn);\n        chk.Parameters.AddWithValue(&quot;?&quot;, serviceCode);\n        object price = chk.ExecuteScalar();\n        if (price == null) return &quot;No such service&quot;;\n\n        OleDbCommand ins = new OleDbCommand(\n          &quot;INSERT INTO BOARDING_SERVICE (BoardingNo, ServiceCode, Qty) VALUES (?, ?, ?)&quot;, conn);\n        ins.Parameters.AddWithValue(&quot;?&quot;, boardingNo);\n        ins.Parameters.AddWithValue(&quot;?&quot;, serviceCode);\n        ins.Parameters.AddWithValue(&quot;?&quot;, qty);\n        int rows = ins.ExecuteNonQuery();\n        msg = rows + &quot; row added, total R&quot; + ((int)price * qty);\n    }\n    catch (OleDbException) { msg = &quot;Already added&quot;; }\n    finally { conn.Close(); }\n    return msg;\n}</pre>", "qs": [{"id": "C4.1", "marks": 2, "q": "State the exact string returned by <code class=\"inline\">addService(101, \"WK\", 3)</code>.", "a": "<p>ExecuteScalar returns 60 (boxed), so price is not null &#10003;. The INSERT adds one row, so <code class=\"inline\">rows = 1</code>. Total = 60 &times; 3 = 180. Result: <b>&ldquo;1 row added, total R180&rdquo;</b> &#10003;.</p>"}, {"id": "C4.2", "marks": 1, "q": "State the exact string returned by <code class=\"inline\">addService(101, \"XX\", 1)</code>, and say whether the connection is closed.", "a": "<p>No row matches &ldquo;XX&rdquo;, so ExecuteScalar returns <code class=\"inline\">null</code> and the method returns <b>&ldquo;No such service&rdquo;</b> from inside the try block &#10003;. The <code class=\"inline\">finally</code> block still runs, so the connection is closed.</p>"}, {"id": "C4.3", "marks": 2, "q": "State the exact string returned by <code class=\"inline\">addService(101, \"GR\", 1)</code> and explain why.", "a": "<p><b>&ldquo;Already added&rdquo;</b> &#10003;. The price lookup succeeds (150), but the row (101, GR) already exists, so the INSERT breaks the composite primary key. The DBMS rejects it, <code class=\"inline\">ExecuteNonQuery()</code> throws an <code class=\"inline\">OleDbException</code> and the catch block sets the message &#10003;.</p>"}, {"id": "C4.4", "marks": 2, "q": "A programmer adds the three INSERT parameters in the order <code class=\"inline\">serviceCode, boardingNo, qty</code>. What happens when <code class=\"inline\">addService(101, \"WK\", 3)</code> is called, and why? [2]", "a": "<p>OleDb matches parameters by <b>position</b>, not by name, so &ldquo;WK&rdquo; is sent to the BoardingNo column and 101 to ServiceCode &#10003;. A text value cannot be stored in a numeric column (data type mismatch), so an OleDbException is thrown, no row is inserted and the method returns the misleading message &ldquo;Already added&rdquo; &#10003;.</p>"}]}, {"type": "qs", "heading": "Question C5 - Report design (12 marks)", "scenario": "Operations Manager <i>Lerato Dube</i> wants to know, each month, which kennels earn the most and how well they are being used, so that she can decide where to invest and how to set the daily rates. Refer to the scenario and the domain class diagram in Question C1.", "qs": [{"id": "C5.1", "marks": 7, "q": "Use the following table to suggest a report that would be useful to the manager described above. <b>Note:</b> redraw the table in your answer book.<div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"paper-tbl\"><tbody><tr><td>Report name:</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report type:</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report format:</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report recipient(s):</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report frequency:</td><td>(&frac12; mark)</td></tr><tr><td>Report rationale:</td><td>(2 marks)</td></tr><tr><td>Decision(s) made as a result of the report:</td><td>(2&frac12; marks)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>", "a": "<p><b>One possible answer</b> (any other reasonable answer is acceptable):</p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"ans-table\"><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Report name</td><td>Kennel Utilisation and Revenue by Month</td></tr><tr><td>Report type</td><td>Summary / management report (aggregates stays, nights and revenue per kennel)</td></tr><tr><td>Report format</td><td>Summary table grouped by kennel and sorted by revenue; optional bar chart of revenue; on screen with PDF / print option</td></tr><tr><td>Report recipient(s)</td><td>Operations Manager (copy to the Owner of PawPrint)</td></tr><tr><td>Report frequency</td><td>Monthly, on the first working day of the next month</td></tr><tr><td>Report rationale</td><td>Shows, for each kennel, the number of stays, nights booked, revenue and occupancy (derived), so the manager can see which kennels earn the most and which stand empty without adding up individual boardings by hand.</td></tr><tr><td>Decision(s) made as a result of the report</td><td><ul><li>Whether to raise or lower the daily rate of under-used or over-demanded kennel sizes</li><li>Whether to add kennels of the most profitable size or convert unused ones</li><li>Which kennels to schedule for maintenance in quiet periods</li><li>Whether to run promotions for low-occupancy months</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Marking: &frac12; each for name, type, format, recipient and frequency; 2 for a rationale that names the problem and the data shown; 2&frac12; for decisions that are concrete actions.</p>"}, {"id": "C5.2", "marks": 3, "q": "Draw a rough <b>prototype</b> of the report you designed in C5.1. It must show a title, the reporting period, column headings with <b>sample data</b>, <b>derived fields</b> and a totals line. [3]", "a": "<div class=\"diagram-wrap wide\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">&harr; scroll sideways to see the whole diagram</div><svg class=\"dg\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 400\" width=\"900\" height=\"400\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Report prototype: Kennel Utilisation and Revenue\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" fill=\"#2a3447\"/></marker><marker id=\"ao\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M1,1 L9,5 L1,9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"900\" height=\"400\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Report prototype (model answer)</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"34\" width=\"860\" height=\"350\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">KENNEL UTILISATION AND REVENUE</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Month: September 2026</text><text x=\"450\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Run date: 01/10/2026</text><text x=\"860\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">For: Operations Manager</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"98\" width=\"840\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#e3e9f2\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Kennel</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Size</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Stays</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Nights</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Daily Rate</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Revenue</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Occupancy %</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"124\" width=\"840\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#bbb\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">K03</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Large</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">3</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">19</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R300</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R5 700</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">63%</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"150\" width=\"840\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#bbb\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">K02</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Medium</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">5</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">24</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R220</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R5 280</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">80%</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"176\" width=\"840\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#bbb\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">K01</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">Small</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">6</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">28</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R180</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R5 040</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">93%</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#1b2230\">...</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"296\" x2=\"870\" y2=\"296\" stroke=\"#2a3447\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">TOTAL</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">14</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">71</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"11.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b2230\">R16 020</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\">Sorted by Revenue (highest first).  Nights = CheckOutDate - CheckInDate;  Revenue = Nights x DailyRate;  Occupancy % = Nights / 30</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"368\" font-size=\"10.5\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"400\" fill=\"#495569\">[derived fields: not stored in the database]</text></svg></div><p><b>Marking guide</b></p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table class=\"flow\"><thead><tr><th>Award marks for</th><th>Marks</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Header block: title, period / run date, recipient</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Body: relevant columns with realistic sample rows, grouped / sorted</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Derived fields (Nights, Revenue, Occupancy %) and a totals line</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><b>Total</b></td><td><b>3</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"}, {"id": "C5.3", "marks": 2, "q": "Write the SQL query that would supply the data for your report. [2]", "a": "<pre class=\"sql\">SELECT k.KennelNo, k.KennelSize,\n       COUNT(b.BoardingNo) AS Stays,\n       SUM(DateDiff(&quot;d&quot;, b.CheckInDate, b.CheckOutDate)) AS Nights,\n       SUM(DateDiff(&quot;d&quot;, b.CheckInDate, b.CheckOutDate) * k.DailyRate) AS Revenue\nFROM KENNEL AS k INNER JOIN BOARDING AS b ON k.KennelNo = b.KennelNo\nWHERE b.CheckInDate &gt;= #2026-09-01# AND b.CheckInDate &lt; #2026-10-01#\nGROUP BY k.KennelNo, k.KennelSize\nORDER BY SUM(DateDiff(&quot;d&quot;, b.CheckInDate, b.CheckOutDate) * k.DailyRate) DESC;</pre><p>&#10003; Correct join of KENNEL to BOARDING on KennelNo with the date range for the month. &#10003; <code class=\"inline\">GROUP BY</code> on the non-aggregated columns with COUNT / SUM and the derived revenue calculation (and an ORDER BY). The comma-join with a WHERE condition is also accepted.</p>"}]}]}]};
